eratorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339813 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339814 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339815 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339816 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339817 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1041 "selection" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339814 13194139535248 true] [17592186339812 1110 #uuid "88e21619-c39f-5b4c-a291-814dec44aada" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339813 1034 "-15\\pi " 13194139535248 true] [17592186339813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535248 true] [17592186339813 1111 #uuid "a3d655fc-fecd-566e-a112-395d1edf56c5" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339814 1034