ame{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{3}{y}\\,i-\\frac{2}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-2-3 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-5)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-5(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-10\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339820 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339821 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339822 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339823 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339824 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1041 "selection" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339822 13194139535248 true] [17592186339819 1110 #uuid "ea096e98-8fd9-55ff-82e5-2cb9154735dd" 13194139535248 true] [17592186339820 1034 "-5\\pi " 13194139535248 true] [17592186339820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535248 true] [17592186339820 1111 #uuid "66b3b284-8ce7-592d-ad66-af8680d66ca4" 13194139535248 